@model string
@*
    The "no records" state of a list, INSIDE the table so the header stays visible: an empty list
    should still show what its columns are, not collapse into a lone sentence.

    colspan="99" rather than the real column count on purpose — the row spans whatever the table
    happens to have, so this partial never needs to know, and adding a column to a list can never
    leave its empty state visually broken. Browsers clamp an oversized colspan to the actual width.
*@
<tr class="list-empty-row">
    <td colspan="99">@Model</td>
</tr>
